{"id": "126622", "name": "מקדמים קבועים הומוגנית – בעיית התחלה, שורשים ממשיים בסימנים שונים (באנגלית)", "defaultgrade": 1, "penalty": 0.1, "options": {"multiplicationsign": "dot", "complexno": "i", "matrixparens": "[", "inversetrig": "cos-1", "logicsymbol": "lang", "sqrtsign": true}, "nhints": 0, "questiontext": "<div dir=\"ltr\" style=\"max-width:980px;font-family:Arial;line-height:1.7\"><div style=\"background:#F4F1F5;border:1px solid #D9D1DD;border-radius:12px;padding:14px 16px\"><p>Find the solution to</p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align:center\">\\[ {{CT:0}} =0 \\]</p><p>subject to</p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align:center\">\\[ y(0) = {{CT:1}} \\]</p><p>and</p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align:center\">\\[ y'(0) = {{CT:2}} \\]</p></div><div style=\"border:1px solid #D9D1DD;border-radius:12px;padding:14px 16px;margin:14px 0;overflow-x:auto\"><div style=\"background:#FAF9FB;border-radius:8px;padding:10px;direction:ltr;text-align:center;unicode-bidi:isolate\">\\(y(t)=\\) [[input:ans1]]</div><div dir=\"ltr\" style=\"direction:ltr;text-align:center;unicode-bidi:isolate;margin-top:6px\">[[validation:ans1]]</div></div></div>", "generalfeedback": "<div dir=\"ltr\" style=\"max-width:980px;font-family:Arial;line-height:1.7\"><div style=\"background:#F4F1F5;border:1px solid #D9D1DD;border-radius:12px;padding:12px 16px;margin-bottom:12px\"><b style=\"color:#4b1f6f\">Outline:</b> Find the general solution from the characteristic equation, then use the two initial conditions to fix the two constants.</div><div style=\"border:1px solid #D9D1DD;border-radius:12px;padding:14px 16px;margin:12px 0;overflow-x:auto\"><b style=\"color:#4b1f6f\">Step 1 — The characteristic equation</b><br>This is a linear homogeneous second-order ODE with constant coefficients, so we look for solutions \\(y=e^{rt}\\). Substituting and dividing by \\(e^{rt}\\) (never zero) gives the characteristic equation<p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align:center\">\\[ {{CT:3}} \\]</p>Factorising, \\({{CT:4}}=0\\), so the roots are \\(r_1={{CT:5}}\\) and \\(r_2={{CT:6}}\\) (distinct and real).</div><div style=\"border:1px solid #D9D1DD;border-radius:12px;padding:14px 16px;margin:12px 0;overflow-x:auto\"><b style=\"color:#4b1f6f\">Step 2 — The general solution</b><br>Hence the general solution is<p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align:center\">\\[ y(t)={{CT:7}} \\]</p></div><div style=\"border:1px solid #D9D1DD;border-radius:12px;padding:14px 16px;margin:12px 0;overflow-x:auto\"><b style=\"color:#4b1f6f\">Step 3 — The initial conditions</b><br>Differentiate and substitute \\(t=0\\) into both conditions:<p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align:center\">\\[ \\begin{cases} {{CT:8}} \\\\ {{CT:9}} \\end{cases} \\]</p>Solving this linear system gives<p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align:center\">\\[ {{CT:10}},\\qquad {{CT:11}} \\]</p>and therefore<p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align:center\">\\[ y(t)={{CT:12}} \\]</p></div></div>", "specificfeedback": "<p>[[feedback:Result]]</p>", "prtcorrect": "<p><span class=\"correct\">Correct answer, well done.</span></p>", "prtpartiallycorrect": "<p><span class=\"partially\">Your answer is partially correct.</span></p>", "prtincorrect": "<p><span class=\"'incorrect\">Incorrect answer.</span></p>", "inputs": [{"name": "ans1", "type": "algebraic", "boxsize": 15, "insertstars": 0, "forbidfloat": true, "forbidwords": "", "allowwords": "", "mustverify": true, "showvalidation": 1, "syntaxhint": "", "syntaxattribute": 0, "options": ""}], "prts": [{"name": "Result", "value": 1, "autosimplify": true, "feedbackstyle": 1, "feedbackvariables": "p:ev(q,y(t)=ans1,nouns,fullratsimp);\n b0:ev(ans1,t=0,fullratsimp);\n dsa:diff(ans1,t);\n b1:ev(dsa,t=0,fullratsimp);", "firstnode": 0, "nodes": [{"name": 0, "answertest": "AlgEquiv", "sans": "p", "tans": "0", "testoptions": null, "quiet": false, "on_true": {"scoremode": "=", "score": 1, "nextnode": 1, "answernote": "Satisfies DE", "feedback": ""}, "on_false": {"scoremode": "=", "score": 0, "nextnode": -1, "answernote": "Fails to satisfy DE", "feedback": "<div dir=\"ltr\">Your answer should satisfy the differential equation, but in fact when we substitute your expression into the differential equation we get \\[{@p@}\\] which is not zero, so you must have done something wrong.</div>"}}, {"name": 1, "answertest": "AlgEquiv", "sans": "b0", "tans": "y0", "testoptions": null, "quiet": false, "on_true": {"scoremode": "+", "score": 0, "nextnode": 2, "answernote": "$y(0)$ correct.", "feedback": ""}, "on_false": {"scoremode": "-", "score": 0.2, "nextnode": 2, "answernote": "$y(0)$ wrong.", "feedback": "<div dir=\"ltr\">Your answer should satisfy \\[ y(0) = {{CT:1}} \\] but does not. When we substitute \\(t=0\\) in your answer we get {@b0@} instead.</div>"}}, {"name": 2, "answertest": "AlgEquiv", "sans": "b1", "tans": "y1", "testoptions": null, "quiet": false, "on_true": {"scoremode": "+", "score": 0, "nextnode": -1, "answernote": "$y'(0)$ correct.", "feedback": ""}, "on_false": {"scoremode": "-", "score": 0.2, "nextnode": -1, "answernote": "$y'(0)$ wrong.", "feedback": "<div dir=\"ltr\">Your answer should satisfy \\[ y'(0) = {{CT:2}} \\] but does not. When we substitute \\(t=0\\) into the derivative of your answer we get {@b1@} instead.</div>"}}]}], "qvnames": ["A", "B", "c1", "c2", "da", "l1", "l2", "q", "solC", "solE1", "solE2", "solYh", "ta", "y0", "y1"], "nvariants": 50}